/* B.E. F.A.S.T. */
"Stroke symptoms come on suddenly. If you notice any one of these signs, call 911 or your local emergency number immediately. Fast treatment can save brain function." = "卒中症状来得很突然。只要发现其中任何一个征兆，请立即拨打 911 或当地急救电话（中国大陆为 120）。及时治疗可以保住大脑功能。";
"Sudden loss of balance or coordination, dizziness, or trouble walking." = "突然失去平衡或协调能力、头晕或行走困难。";
"Sudden blurred or double vision, or loss of vision in one or both eyes." = "突然视物模糊或重影，或一只眼或双眼失明。";
"One side of the face droops or feels numb. The smile may look uneven." = "一侧面部下垂或发麻，笑起来可能不对称。";
"Sudden weakness or numbness in an arm or leg, often on one side of the body." = "手臂或腿突然无力或麻木，通常在身体一侧。";
"Slurred speech, trouble speaking or understanding, or sudden confusion." = "说话含糊、说话或理解困难，或突然意识混乱。";
"Call 911 right away, even if the symptoms go away. Note the time they started." = "即使症状消失，也要立即拨打 911 或当地急救电话（中国大陆为 120）。记下症状开始的时间。";

/* Types of stroke */
"Types of stroke" = "卒中类型";
"Strokes are caused either by a blockage or by bleeding. A TIA is a temporary warning." = "卒中由血管堵塞或出血引起。TIA 是一种暂时性的警告。";
"Ischemic stroke" = "缺血性卒中";
"The most common type, about 87% of strokes." = "最常见的类型，约占卒中的 87%。";
"An ischemic stroke happens when a blood clot or narrowed artery blocks blood flow to part of the brain." = "当血栓或狭窄的动脉阻断流向部分大脑的血液时，就会发生缺血性卒中。";
"Clot-dissolving medicine works best when given within a few hours of the first symptoms." = "溶栓药物在首次出现症状后数小时内使用效果最好。";
"Doctors may also remove large clots with a catheter (thrombectomy)." = "医生也可以用导管取出较大的血栓（取栓术）。";
"Every minute counts, so call 911 or your local emergency number right away." = "分秒必争，请立即拨打 911 或当地急救电话（中国大陆为 120）。";
"Hemorrhagic stroke" = "出血性卒中";
"Less common, about 13% of strokes, but often more severe." = "较少见，约占卒中的 13%，但通常更严重。";
"A hemorrhagic stroke happens when a weakened blood vessel breaks and bleeds into or around the brain, raising pressure and damaging tissue." = "当脆弱的血管破裂，血液流入脑内或脑周围时，就会发生出血性卒中，导致颅内压升高并损伤脑组织。";
"High blood pressure is a common cause." = "高血压是常见原因。";
"Treatment may include lowering blood pressure and surgery to stop the bleeding or relieve pressure." = "治疗可能包括降压，以及通过手术止血或减轻压力。";
"Aneurysms can be clipped or coiled to seal the vessel." = "动脉瘤可通过夹闭或弹簧圈栓塞来封闭血管。";
"Transient ischemic attack" = "短暂性脑缺血发作";
"A \"mini-stroke\" with symptoms that go away." = "一种症状会消失的“小中风”。";
"A TIA is a brief blockage of blood flow to the brain. Its symptoms are the same as a stroke but usually last only minutes." = "TIA 是流向大脑的血液短暂受阻。症状与卒中相同，但通常只持续几分钟。";
"A TIA is a warning sign that a stroke may follow." = "TIA 是一个警示信号，之后可能发生卒中。";
"It needs emergency care, even if the symptoms are gone." = "即使症状已经消失，也需要紧急就医。";
"Treating the cause can prevent a future stroke." = "治疗病因可以预防将来发生卒中。";

/* Risk factors */
"Risk factors" = "风险因素";
"Some conditions and habits make a stroke more likely. Many of them can be treated or changed." = "某些疾病和习惯会增加卒中的可能。其中许多可以治疗或改变。";
"High blood pressure" = "高血压";
"The leading cause of stroke. Over time it damages and weakens blood vessels." = "卒中的首要原因。长期下来会损伤并削弱血管。";
"Diabetes" = "糖尿病";
"High blood sugar damages blood vessels and makes clots more likely." = "高血糖会损伤血管，并更容易形成血栓。";
"Heart disease" = "心脏病";
"Conditions such as atrial fibrillation (AFib) can cause clots that travel to the brain." = "心房颤动等疾病可能形成血栓，并随血流进入大脑。";
"Smoking" = "吸烟";
"Damages blood vessels and raises blood pressure." = "损伤血管并升高血压。";
"Sleep apnea" = "睡眠呼吸暂停";
"Repeated pauses in breathing during sleep strain the heart and blood vessels." = "睡眠中反复出现呼吸暂停会加重心脏和血管的负担。";
"Drug use" = "吸毒";
"Drugs such as cocaine and amphetamines can trigger a stroke, even in young people." = "可卡因和苯丙胺等毒品可能诱发卒中，即使是年轻人也不例外。";

/* Prevention */
"Lower your risk" = "降低风险";
"Most strokes are linked to risk factors you can manage. These habits help at any age." = "大多数卒中与可控的风险因素有关。这些习惯在任何年龄都有帮助。";
"Control blood pressure" = "控制血压";
"Check it regularly and take medicine as prescribed." = "定期测量，并按医嘱服药。";
"Manage blood sugar" = "控制血糖";
"Keep diabetes under control with your care team." = "与医疗团队一起控制好糖尿病。";
"Manage cholesterol" = "控制胆固醇";
"Ask your doctor how often to get it checked." = "问问医生多久检查一次。";
"Quit smoking and tobacco" = "戒烟";
"Your risk starts dropping soon after you quit." = "戒烟后不久，风险就开始下降。";
"Stay active" = "保持运动";
"Aim for about 30 minutes of moderate activity most days." = "大多数日子进行约 30 分钟中等强度活动。";
"Eat a heart-healthy diet" = "健康饮食护心脏";
"More vegetables, fruit and whole grains; less salt and processed food." = "多吃蔬菜、水果和全谷物；少吃盐和加工食品。";
"Keep a healthy weight" = "保持健康体重";
"Even modest weight loss can lower blood pressure." = "即使只减轻一点体重，也能降低血压。";
"Sleep well" = "睡个好觉";
"Aim for 7 to 9 hours, and get checked if you snore heavily." = "每晚睡 7 到 9 小时；如果鼾声很重，请去检查。";

/* Treatments */
"Treatment depends on the type of stroke and how quickly it begins. The sooner, the better." = "治疗取决于卒中类型以及开始治疗的速度。越早越好。";
"Clot-dissolving medicine" = "溶栓药物";
"Medicine given through an IV to break up a clot." = "通过静脉输注、用于溶解血栓的药物。";
"For ischemic stroke, a clot-dissolving medicine such as tPA can restore blood flow to the brain." = "对于缺血性卒中，tPA 等溶栓药物可以恢复大脑的血流。";
"Works best when started within 3 to 4.5 hours of the first symptoms." = "在首次出现症状后 3 到 4.5 小时内开始使用效果最好。";
"Can improve recovery and reduce disability." = "可以改善恢复并减少残疾。";
"Not used when there is a high risk of bleeding, such as after recent surgery." = "出血风险较高时（例如近期做过手术）不使用。";
"Mechanical thrombectomy" = "机械取栓术";
"A catheter procedure to remove a large clot." = "用导管取出大血栓的手术。";
"A thin tube is guided through an artery to the brain, where doctors remove the clot directly." = "医生将一根细管沿动脉送到大脑，直接取出血栓。";
"Can be done up to 24 hours after symptoms start for some patients." = "部分患者在症状出现后 24 小时内仍可进行。";
"Often used together with clot-dissolving medicine for strokes in large arteries." = "对于大动脉卒中，常与溶栓药物联合使用。";
"Restores blood flow quickly to limit brain damage." = "迅速恢复血流，减少脑损伤。";
"Surgery for bleeding" = "出血手术";
"Procedures to stop bleeding and relieve pressure." = "用于止血和减轻压力的手术。";
"In a hemorrhagic stroke, surgery may be needed to stop the bleeding and lower pressure on the brain." = "出血性卒中可能需要手术来止血并降低对大脑的压力。";
"An aneurysm can be clipped or coiled to seal the bleeding vessel." = "可通过夹闭或弹簧圈栓塞动脉瘤来封闭出血的血管。";
"A craniotomy can remove pooled blood and relieve pressure." = "开颅手术可以清除积血并减轻压力。";
"Quick treatment helps prevent further brain injury." = "及时治疗有助于防止大脑进一步受损。";
"Rehabilitation" = "康复";
"Therapy to regain skills after a stroke." = "卒中后帮助恢复能力的治疗。";
"Recovery often continues for months. Rehabilitation helps people relearn movement, speech and everyday tasks." = "恢复往往持续数月。康复能帮助患者重新学习活动、说话和日常事务。";
"May include physical, occupational and speech therapy." = "可能包括物理治疗、作业治疗和言语治疗。";
"Starting early, while still in the hospital, tends to help." = "尽早开始，在住院期间就开始，通常更有帮助。";
"Family and caregivers are an important part of recovery." = "家人和照护者是康复的重要组成部分。";

